# "Each player shuffles their hand and graveyard into their library, then draws seven": Bot1's Lightning Bolt (cast at Bot2)
# and its sacrificed Black Lotus are in the graveyard when Echo of Eons resolves and go into the library, while the Echo itself,
# still on the stack as it resolves, is not in the graveyard to be shuffled (CR 608.2n: it goes there afterwards). So Bot1's library of
# 10 becomes 12, and after the draw of seven it holds 5; the graveyard is the Echo alone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Echo of Eons
Lightning Bolt
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x22

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Echo of Eons.Cast
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Graveyard = Echo of Eons
Bot1.Hand.Count = 7
Bot1.Library.Count = 5
Bot2.Hand.Count = 7
Bot2.Library.Count = 15
